{"docs": [{"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-pytorch-c-api-documentation:ee9f82fa", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation", "heading_path": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "This directory contains the source for PyTorch's C++ API documentation, built with Sphinx, Breathe, and Doxygen."}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-pytorch-c-api-documentation-how-it-works:62161728", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "How it works", "heading_path": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation > How it works", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "C++ headers \u2500\u2500\u2192 Doxygen \u2500\u2500\u2192 XML \u2500\u2500\u2192 Breathe \u2500\u2500\u2192 Sphinx \u2500\u2500\u2192 HTML  \u2191 \u2191  Doxyfile Markdown files with  (which headers) Breathe directives (MyST)"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-pytorch-c-api-documentation-building:9b529bb7", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Building", "heading_path": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation > Building", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "bash make html # Build Doxygen XML + Sphinx HTML make doxygen # Build Doxygen XML only make clean # Clean build artifacts"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-pytorch-c-api-documentation-contributing-to-the-c-docs-adding-a-new-a:abedc483", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Adding a new API", "heading_path": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation > Contributing to the C++ docs > Adding a new API", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "1. **Ensure the header is in the Doxyfile** \u2014 check that source/Doxyfile INPUT  includes the header file or its parent directory. If not, add it:"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-pytorch-c-api-documentation-contributing-to-the-c-docs-which-directiv:6e26f6ab", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Which directive to use", "heading_path": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation > Contributing to the C++ docs > Which directive to use", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "Use Breathe directives to pull documentation from Doxygen XML. These render the full C++ signature, doc comments, parameters, and members automatically."}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-pytorch-c-api-documentation-contributing-to-the-c-docs-when-breathe-d:a3731854", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "When Breathe directives don't work", "heading_path": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation > Contributing to the C++ docs > When Breathe directives don't work", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "- **TORCH_MODULE holder classes** (e.g., Conv2d, Linear): The TORCH_MODULE()  macro generates these, but Doxygen can't index them. Document the *Impl class  instead (e.g., Conv2dImpl) \u2014 it contains all the actual methods."}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-pytorch-c-api-documentation-contributing-to-the-c-docs-source-file-st:68b53daa", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Source file structure", "heading_path": "PyTorch C++ API Documentation > Contributing to the C++ docs > Source file structure", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "Each .md file under source/api/ documents one topic area using MyST Markdown. The typical pattern:"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-section-name:be1f1171", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Section Name", "heading_path": "Page Title > Section Name", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "**Nesting directives:** When a directive contains other directives or code blocks, the outer fence must use more backticks than the inner ones:"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-section-name-writing-doc-comments-in-c-headers:9d5b6117", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Writing doc comments in C++ headers", "heading_path": "Page Title > Section Name > Writing doc comments in C++ headers", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "cpp /// Applies a linear transformation to the incoming data: :math:y = xA^T + b. /// /// @code{.cpp} /// auto linear = torch::nn::Linear(torch::nn::LinearOptions(10, 5)); /// auto output = linear->forward(input); /// @endcode /// /// @note The weight matrix is transposed\u2026"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-coverage-checking:9016e8f0", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Coverage checking", "heading_path": "Page Title > Coverage checking", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "bash make coverage # Build docs + run coverage check make coverage-only # Run coverage check without rebuilding"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-coverage-checking-how-coverage-discovery-works:c4e31e0c", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "How coverage discovery works", "heading_path": "Page Title > Coverage checking > How coverage discovery works", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "The script parses build/xml/index.xml to find all classes, structs, functions, and macros that Doxygen indexed. It then:"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-coverage-checking-excluding-internal-apis-from-coverage:622e3bb5", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Excluding internal APIs from coverage", "heading_path": "Page Title > Coverage checking > Excluding internal APIs from coverage", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "Not everything in Doxygen XML is public API. The script has three exclusion mechanisms:"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-coverage-checking-including-internal-apis-that-are-actuall:970195f4", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Including \"internal\" APIs that are actually public", "heading_path": "Page Title > Coverage checking > Including \"internal\" APIs that are actually public", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "Some APIs live in internal-looking namespaces but are widely used by external developers. To track these for documentation coverage, add them to INCLUDED_SYMBOLS in check_coverage.py:"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-coverage-checking-html-formatting-checks:e5f5e057", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "HTML formatting checks", "heading_path": "Page Title > Coverage checking > HTML formatting checks", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "The script also checks built HTML for: - Unresolved Breathe directives (\"Cannot find class/struct/function\") - Raw directive text in output (build failures) - Sphinx \"problematic\" nodes (broken references) - Near-empty API pages"}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-coverage-checking-coverxygen-optional:a95a8bf1", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "coverxygen (optional)", "heading_path": "Page Title > Coverage checking > coverxygen (optional)", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "This runs coverxygen on the Doxygen XML to measure what percentage of C++ symbols have doc comments in the source code. This is complementary to file coverage \u2014 it tells you which headers need more doc comments, not which symbols need Sphinx directives."}, {"chunk_id": "pytorch:latest:cpp-readme-page-title-known-issues:bc750b4b", "vendor": "pytorch", "version": "latest", "title": "Known issues", "heading_path": "Page Title > Known issues", "path": "cpp/README", "source_url": "https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp/README.html", "license": "MIT", "attribution": "\u00a9 pytorch/pytorch contributors \u2014 MIT License, via docs-mesh", "last_updated": "2026-08-31", "snippet": "- **\\rst/\\endrst rendering** \u2014 Some C++ headers use Doxygen's \\rst alias to  embed RST in doc comments. When a single doc comment has multiple \\rst/\\endrst  blocks, Doxygen generates malformed XML and Breathe renders them as raw text.  Avoid using :members: on classes with this\u2026"}], "postings": {"pytorch": [[0, 9.516672534990692], [1, 3.5687522006215096], [2, 3.5687522006215096], [3, 3.5687522006215096], [4, 3.5687522006215096], [5, 3.5687522006215096], [6, 3.5687522006215096]], "api": [[0, 7.644091560219491], [1, 3.8220457801097454], [2, 2.866534335082309], [3, 11.466137340329237], [4, 2.866534335082309], [5, 2.866534335082309], [6, 3.8220457801097454], [8, 0.9555114450274363], [11, 1.9110228900548727], [13, 0.9555114450274363]], "documentation": [[0, 8.17320998025585], [1, 5.108256237659906], [2, 3.064953742595944], [3, 3.064953742595944], [4, 4.086604990127925], [5, 3.064953742595944], [6, 3.064953742595944], [8, 1.0216512475319812], [12, 1.0216512475319812]], "this": [[0, 1.8458266904983307], [14, 3.6916533809966614], [15, 1.8458266904983307]], "directory": [[0, 2.1972245773362196], [3, 2.1972245773362196]], "contains": [[0, 1.6094379124341003], [5, 1.6094379124341003], [7, 1.6094379124341003], [8, 1.6094379124341003]], "source": [[0, 1.0986122886681098], [1, 3.295836866004329], [3, 2.1972245773362196], [4, 1.0986122886681098], [6, 8.788898309344878], [9, 1.0986122886681098], [14, 1.0986122886681098], [15, 1.0986122886681098]], "built": [[0, 2.1972245773362196], [13, 2.1972245773362196]], "sp